  "explanation": {
    "short": "The sign ि is a short \"i\" and it is written BEFORE its letter, though you say it after: रवि is ra-vi and किताब is ki-tāb. The signs ु and ू sit under the letter: ु is a short \"u\" (सुबह) and ू is a long \"oo\" (दूध).",
    "more": "Short and long vowels are different sounds in Hindi: ि and ी, ु and ू. Look at the length of the sign: the longer sign is the longer sound. In रुपये the middle \"a\" is hardly said: rup-ye. A vowel at the start of a word, or after another vowel, has its own letter: इ is the short \"i\" of बाइबल."
  },
